# #664: a top-level map call whose outs have a file param, which fork "a"
# leaves null. mrp's PostProcess makes each fork's outs/<key>/ before it
# reads the fork's values (core/post_process.go processStructOuts), so it
# publishes an empty outs/a/ beside outs/b/result.json. The other
# invocations fork over an array (array.mro), publish a file only inside a
# struct (struct.mro), disable the stage of one fork (disabled.mro), and
# publish no file (nofile.mro), for which mrp makes no outs/.
@include "stages.mro"

map call MAKE(
    v = split {
        "a": "none",
        "b": "file",
    },
)
